 step in a program again this is a  management tool for how your functions  are called within node.js  so what is the difference between fork  and spawn methods in node.js  so the essential difference between the  two of them is that if you use the fork  method it will actually trigger and  create a new instance of the v8 engine  the engine running nodejs and will then  run the application in that new instance  with spawn  it's somewhat similar it doesn't  actually generate a new v8 instance so  it's actually creating a new process but  it's within the same v8 instance as the  previous application that it was spawned  from  explain to me what is the use of buffer  class in node.js  so with the buffer class what you're  looking at doing is you're actually  controlling the raw data of a set of  arrays and integers  and the memory allocation outside of the  v8 heap buffer class is used because  pure javascript is not compatible with  binary data  what is piping in node.js  so  piping is the ability to connect the  output of one stream to another stream  that could be a data stream it could be  any stream that you're working with  but it does normally get used to pass  data from one stream to another  so what are some of the flags used in  the rewrite operation files  so r dash is used for read w's for  opening a file for writing  a dash is opening a file for appending  so the collection that you have here you  don't have to really memorize all of  them but to have a few of them  in the back of your mind is always a  good  reference point  so how would you open a file using  node.js  so  the syntax you would use would be  the  fs.open and that would then open up a  file  explain to me what callback hell is  so callback hell also known as the  pyramid of doom is when you have too  many  nested unreadable and unmanageable  callbacks intensively cycle within each  other and they're constantly reading to  each other and they're not able to  resolve the solution  and uh this